<title>SOUTH KOREA: Dong Yang to buy back 69,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Dong Yang to buy back 69,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Dong Yang Tinplate Co Ltd said on Friday it would buy back 69,000 of its own common shares on the Seoul bourse to boost stock prices.  </p>
<p>A company statement said the buy-back, representing 3.01 percent of Dong Yang's total outstanding shares, would be implemented from October 14 to January 13 next year.</p>
<p>Daishin, Dongsuh and Dongwon Securities will handle the purchase.</p>
<p>The statement said the shares would be bought at the previous day's closing price.</p>
<p>Shares in Dong Yang rose 500 won to 26,300 just after Friday's opening.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
